# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:199
js-kind-note-a-gap-is-an-epoch = A gap is an epoch with too few relays in view for a fix.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:533
js-kind-note-a-helmert-transform-is-the = A Helmert transform is the seven-parameter shift, rotation and scale between two reference frames.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:345
js-kind-note-a-low-earth-orbit-leo = A low Earth orbit (LEO) satellite crosses the sky in minutes, so its C/N0 (carrier-to-noise density ratio) rises and falls in a bell; a GNSS satellite barely moves in the same time.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:422
js-kind-note-a-receiver-independent-exchange-format = A Receiver Independent Exchange Format (RINEX) 4 style record. The LEO record types are a Kshana extension, as the header says.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:450
js-kind-note-a-single-pass-fixes-the = A single pass fixes the along-track direction far better than the cross-track one.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:352
js-kind-note-aos-is-acquisition-of-signal = AOS is acquisition of signal, TCA the time of closest approach and LOS loss of signal.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:165
js-kind-note-c-n0-is-the-carrier = C/N0 is the carrier-to-noise density ratio. A band under the receiver's tracking threshold has lost lock.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:306
js-kind-note-cells-are-the-code-and = Cells are the code and Doppler bins a cold search must test.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:359
js-kind-note-cold-is-a-first-fix = Cold is a first fix with no prior knowledge; hot is a fix soon after the last one.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:216
js-kind-note-dilution-of-precision-dop-scales = Dilution of precision (DOP) scales a range error into a position error: G is geometric, P position, H horizontal, V vertical. Percentiles are over every grid point and epoch.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:458
js-kind-note-drawn-at-the-strongest-signal = Drawn at the strongest signal level of the run. A gap is a stretch with no satellite in view.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:187
js-kind-note-each-body-carries-its-own = Each body carries its own evidence label. Light time is one way, from the observer named in the scenario.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:256
js-kind-note-each-row-is-one-full = Each row is one full engine run of the swept scenario.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:407
js-kind-note-each-rule-is-a-switch = Each rule is a switch to a newer message in the middle of the pass.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:299
js-kind-note-each-signal-is-drawn-about = Each signal is drawn about its own centre frequency. A gap is a spectral null.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:168
js-kind-note-eirp-is-the-equivalent-isotropically = EIRP is the equivalent isotropically radiated power.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:236
js-kind-note-every-phase-is-an-ordinary = Every phase is an ordinary scenario run. The hashes identify each member's input and its result document.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:408
js-kind-note-iod-is-the-issue-of = IOD is the issue of data: the message's serial number.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:167
js-kind-note-j-s-is-the-jammer = J/S is the jammer-to-signal power ratio. Tracking fraction is the share of the run the band stays above the threshold.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:264
js-kind-note-p05-p50-and-p95-are = p05, p50 and p95 are the 5th, 50th and 95th percentiles. ci95 is the 95% confidence interval on the mean.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:301
js-kind-note-parameters-are-public-with-a = Parameters are PUBLIC (with a source), REPRESENTATIVE or WORKSHOP, as each preset states.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:484
js-kind-note-precise-point-positioning-ppp-converges = Precise point positioning (PPP) converges when the error stays under the criterion. NEES is the normalised estimation error squared, a filter-consistency check.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:383
js-kind-note-sisre-defined = SISRE is the signal-in-space range error: what the broadcast message adds to a user's range. Here it is the message's representation error against the engine's own truth orbit.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:468
js-kind-note-sisre-is-the-signal-in = SISRE is the signal-in-space range error assumed for each system's broadcast orbit and clock.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:312
js-kind-note-ssc-is-the-spectral-separation = SSC is the spectral separation coefficient: how much of one signal's power falls inside the other's receiver. A dash means the two do not overlap.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:507
js-kind-note-the-chain-runs-the-signal = The chain runs the signal, pass, navigation-message, positioning and precise-positioning stages in order. Each row is a number one stage computed and the next one used.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:366
js-kind-note-the-doppler-and-pass-geometry = The Doppler and pass-geometry monitor compares measured range rates with those predicted from the orbits. The rule marks the spoofer's onset.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:171
js-kind-note-the-engine-draws-its-spectrum = The engine draws its spectrum model as in-phase and quadrature (IQ) samples at one instant and estimates the spectrum back from them. The same samples are the SigMF (Signal Metadata Format) export.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:417
js-kind-note-the-engine-s-own-documented = The engine's own documented binary frame, closed by a 24-bit cyclic redundancy check (CRC-24Q).

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:303
js-kind-note-the-gabor-root-mean-square = The Gabor (root-mean-square) bandwidth sets how sharply a signal can be ranged on.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:308
js-kind-note-the-largest-jammer-to-signal = The largest jammer-to-signal ratio (J/S) each signal tracks through, for a continuous-wave (CW), a matched-spectrum and a wideband jammer.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:189
js-kind-note-the-shapiro-delay-is-the = The Shapiro delay is the extra light time from the Sun's gravity along the path.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:176
js-kind-note-the-spectrum-kind-and-the = The spectrum kind and the jamming kind compute the same link two ways; the last column is their difference.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:495
js-kind-note-time-of-arrival-toa-ranging = Time-of-arrival (TOA) ranging on a non-terrestrial network (NTN) downlink: a wider signal ranges more sharply.

# 2026-10-01-studio-rebuild/lib/kinds.mjs:421
js-kind-note-what-half-a-least-significant = What half a least-significant bit (LSB) of each field costs in position and in clock, as range.

